Task Guide:

Task make_2_lvl3:
Propose a retrosynthesis route to synthesize the molecule with SMILES COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O. The leaves on the retrosynthesis tree should be commercially available chemicals. The price of all the chemical cannot exceed $405.0. The final route should not surpass 1 steps.

Required submission format:
Submit a JSON object representing the retrosynthesis route. It must follow the same JSON format as the next example: `{
  "type": "mol",
  "smiles": "CO",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "reaction",
      "template_id": 1234,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "BrC"
        },
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "[OH-]"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}`.



You must think what to do next. You can use some of the tools available in the system.

When you think that the task is completed, you can submit the answer.
For that, answer with: "Final Answer: <your answer>". It is very important to follow this format.

The route is valid, the step is verified chemically, and dimethyl dicarbonate is confirmed commercially available at $128 (well under $405). This is a single-step esterification of the carboxylic acid precursor.

Final Answer: 
```json
{
  "type": "mol",
  "smiles": "COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "reaction",
      "template_id": 222683,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "COC(=O)OC(=O)OC"
        },
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "O=C1C[C@@]2(C(=O)O)CC=CC[C@@H]12"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This is a one-step methyl esterification: the bicyclic keto-carboxylic acid (O=C1C[C@@]2(C(=O)O)CC=CC[C@@H]12) is converted to its methyl ester using dimethyl dicarbonate (COC(=O)OC(=O)OC), which is commercially available at $128 (within the $405 budget). The retrosynthetic step was verified valid (verify_step = True) and the route structure passes schema validation.
